1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:07,256
THIS PROGRAM CONTAINS
AI-GENERATED CONTENT

2
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:09,259
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

3
00:00:18,769 --> 00:00:21,521
GRAND PRINCE HWIRYEONG

4
00:00:21,522 --> 00:00:23,689
The national coffers are empty,

5
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:26,318
but the powerful grow richer by the day.

6
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:29,655
Taxes wrung
from the people's blood and sweat

7
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:33,616
are being pocketed along the way.

8
00:00:33,617 --> 00:00:34,743
Lord Yun.

9
00:00:35,494 --> 00:00:37,578
Are you not in a position

10
00:00:37,579 --> 00:00:39,831
to advise His Majesty to do what is right?

11
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:43,918
I have heard that while the people starve,

12
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:46,213
the court is falsifying records
of abundant harvests.

13
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:49,799
For the sake of the people,

14
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,217
as your humble servant,

15
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:52,886
I shall dare to write a petition.

16
00:00:57,391 --> 00:00:59,393
[♪ theme song playing]

17
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:06,607
MURDER CLUB: LIAR'S TABLE

18
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:09,026
I'll be strategic and open one more.

19
00:01:09,027 --> 00:01:10,444
- You had two?
- Yes.

20
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:11,529
PLENTY OF BONUS CARDS

21
00:01:11,530 --> 00:01:14,156
- [Igyeong] He'll open them all.
- At least he's handsome.

22
00:01:14,157 --> 00:01:16,534
- I like him.
- [laughing]

23
00:01:16,535 --> 00:01:17,578
Gosh, ma'am.

24
00:01:18,161 --> 00:01:19,245
What's that?

25
00:01:19,246 --> 00:01:20,705
- Oh, my.
- [Suyeon] "Yun Igyeong…"

26
00:01:20,706 --> 00:01:23,457
- [contestants] "Yun Igyeong."
- "Eliminate."

27
00:01:23,458 --> 00:01:24,542
- "Office."
- "Office."

28
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:27,296
[gasps] They heard
you were being eliminated.

29
00:01:27,963 --> 00:01:30,506
Dad, someone tried to eliminate you.

30
00:01:30,507 --> 00:01:32,217
Gosh, I nearly died.

31
00:01:32,718 --> 00:01:36,012
- Kill Yun Igyeong and gain office.
- They meant to kill me instead?

32
00:01:36,013 --> 00:01:37,930
- I think so.
- That says--

33
00:01:37,931 --> 00:01:39,974
Gosh, this is really fun.

34
00:01:39,975 --> 00:01:41,893
Number nine, please.

35
00:01:43,353 --> 00:01:44,437
PICTURE OF THE CRIME SCENE

36
00:01:44,438 --> 00:01:46,439
- [Bokgil] What's that?
- A picture?

37
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:47,732
It's the scene of the crime.

38
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:48,859
[Igyeong] It's a pair of shoes!

39
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,901
Look closely at the footprints.

40
00:01:50,902 --> 00:01:52,362
- Where are they headed?
- Shoes?

41
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:55,406
They came out from here
and walked that way.

42
00:01:55,407 --> 00:01:57,451
This is the kitchen.

43
00:01:57,951 --> 00:02:00,036
That's where the trail of blood started.

44
00:02:00,037 --> 00:02:01,787
[Suyeon] <i>Someone was in the kitchen.</i>

45
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,122
THE KITCHEN IS THE SOURCE

46
00:02:03,123 --> 00:02:05,458
- Where were you at that time?
- [Musoe] Lady Yun.

47
00:02:05,459 --> 00:02:06,876
I know that you planned

48
00:02:06,877 --> 00:02:09,253
to run away in the middle of the night.

49
00:02:09,254 --> 00:02:10,755
Did you not meet Bokgil?

50
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:12,632
I told you I was just in my room.

51
00:02:12,633 --> 00:02:13,716
- The whole night?
- Yes.

52
00:02:13,717 --> 00:02:16,010
- But--
- I never left the house.

53
00:02:16,011 --> 00:02:18,179
You only planned to run away?

54
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:22,224
I planned to run away,
but I never actually left the house.

55
00:02:22,225 --> 00:02:24,769
If you were in your room,
where was Bokgil?

56
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:27,521
I was just out for a walk.

57
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:28,689
I like exercising at night.

58
00:02:28,690 --> 00:02:30,524
- I'm serious.
- [Suyeon] You took a walk?

59
00:02:30,525 --> 00:02:32,401
- That's so suspicious.
- I just…

60
00:02:32,402 --> 00:02:34,862
[Bokgil] <i>It was a nice, moonlit night
so I did some light exercise.</i>

61
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:36,364
- <i>Exercise under the moonlight?</i>
- <i>Yes.</i>

62
00:02:36,365 --> 00:02:39,075
BOKGIL, A MAN OF MYSTERY

63
00:02:39,076 --> 00:02:40,743
One thing's for sure.

64
00:02:40,744 --> 00:02:42,870
Bokgil is no ordinary slave.

65
00:02:42,871 --> 00:02:46,290
- No, he isn't.
- [Suyeon] I think someone higher up

66
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:48,584
hired him to infiltrate as a slave--

67
00:02:48,585 --> 00:02:50,795
- [laughs] Oh, please.
- He's an undercover slave.

68
00:02:50,796 --> 00:02:54,298
If I were that capable,
I would already be sitting pretty.

69
00:02:54,299 --> 00:02:56,050
But you were out walking

70
00:02:56,051 --> 00:02:57,927
at the time of the crime.

71
00:02:57,928 --> 00:02:59,011
[Suyeon] Exactly.

72
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:02,139
The time of my walk and the murder

73
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:03,891
puts all of us within those confines

74
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,142
- by that logic.
- [Suyeon] That's true.

75
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:07,269
I have a feeling that Bokgil

76
00:03:07,270 --> 00:03:09,689
is not just a slave.

77
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:12,983
I grew up with Musoe,

78
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:16,862
<i>but Bokgil moved in with us
after we were exiled.</i>

79
00:03:16,863 --> 00:03:18,572
<i>And he has many skills.</i>

80
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:22,952
That's why I think he might be
someone from the outside.

81
00:03:22,953 --> 00:03:25,371
Bokgil. You know…

82
00:03:25,372 --> 00:03:27,373
we agreed to run away together, right?

83
00:03:27,374 --> 00:03:28,457
Yes, we did.

84
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:30,251
But what I am wondering is,

85
00:03:30,252 --> 00:03:32,420
are you really a slave?

86
00:03:32,421 --> 00:03:34,964
Of course, I am a slave right now.

87
00:03:34,965 --> 00:03:37,174
But I am a dignified slave.

88
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:40,136
Did someone order you to kill my dad?

89
00:03:40,137 --> 00:03:42,596
It was not to kill--

90
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:44,807
I'm on your side! I like you.

91
00:03:44,808 --> 00:03:46,809
So right now, you and I

92
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:48,686
need to be honest with each other.

93
00:03:48,687 --> 00:03:51,439
I do not deal in such matters.

94
00:03:51,440 --> 00:03:53,649
- You said you were out for a walk.
- Yes.

95
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:55,443
There must have been noises.

96
00:03:55,444 --> 00:03:56,986
Didn't you hear anything?

97
00:03:56,987 --> 00:03:59,905
I did hear a scream,

98
00:03:59,906 --> 00:04:02,783
but I arrived on the scene
after it happened.

99
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:05,619
- I was a little distance away.
- [sighs] That's your story?

100
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:06,621
[Igyeong] <i>The important thing is,</i>

101
00:04:07,205 --> 00:04:08,956
I keep wondering

102
00:04:08,957 --> 00:04:10,082
who my daughter really is.

103
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:12,668
Because why was there a record in her room

104
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:16,630
- about a baby with a blue mark?
- Right.

105
00:04:16,631 --> 00:04:19,592
[Igyeong] <i>The victim also had
a blue mark on his hand.</i>

106
00:04:19,593 --> 00:04:22,636
If it is a genetic mark,

107
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:25,306
<i>it ties back to the evidence
the shaman showed us</i>

108
00:04:25,307 --> 00:04:26,850
about the babies being switched.

109
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:28,768
Yes.

110
00:04:28,769 --> 00:04:30,478
[Igyeong] So, Yun Suyeon…

111
00:04:30,479 --> 00:04:32,354
- [Hwiryeong] She isn't your daughter?
- That's right.

112
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:33,981
- Not my daughter.
- Not biologically.

113
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:38,069
And the local female innkeeper testified

114
00:04:38,779 --> 00:04:41,530
that a strange figure came by
looking for Yun Suyeon,

115
00:04:41,531 --> 00:04:45,201
but importantly,
they knew what she looked like.

116
00:04:45,202 --> 00:04:47,787
So the victim could be Yun Suyeon's

117
00:04:47,788 --> 00:04:49,914
- real father?
- Or the person she was switched with.

118
00:04:49,915 --> 00:04:51,582
- Right.
- It could also be her real father.

119
00:04:51,583 --> 00:04:52,917
Mmm…

120
00:04:52,918 --> 00:04:55,920
So I guess she is not your daughter.

121
00:04:55,921 --> 00:04:57,463
I think it is very likely

122
00:04:57,464 --> 00:04:59,131
that my child was switched.

123
00:04:59,132 --> 00:05:00,884
Then what about the switched child?

124
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:02,718
Who are they?

125
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:04,136
[Igyeong] I am not sure.

126
00:05:04,137 --> 00:05:05,138
[Suyeon] <i>By the way,</i>

127
00:05:05,722 --> 00:05:07,139
did you have a fling with Musoe?

128
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:08,224
No, I did not.

129
00:05:08,225 --> 00:05:09,892
I thought she was a man.

130
00:05:09,893 --> 00:05:11,227
That's how little I cared.

131
00:05:11,228 --> 00:05:13,646
But I suspect something
was going on between you

132
00:05:13,647 --> 00:05:15,356
because she wrote you a love note

133
00:05:15,357 --> 00:05:16,607
and even drew a heart on it.

134
00:05:16,608 --> 00:05:18,317
There was nothing between us.

135
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,027
Come on. She has nothing on you.

136
00:05:20,028 --> 00:05:22,822
Do not compare yourself to Musoe.

137
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:26,242
I dedicated myself to serving your father,

138
00:05:26,243 --> 00:05:28,369
and then you and I became involved,

139
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:30,538
so I thought it was destiny

140
00:05:30,539 --> 00:05:33,999
and hoped to get away
and live happily together.

141
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,586
Well, what are your thoughts so far?

142
00:05:37,295 --> 00:05:39,463
Is there someone you suspect?

143
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:40,548
To be honest,

144
00:05:40,549 --> 00:05:42,050
Lord Yun

145
00:05:42,801 --> 00:05:45,427
suspects you the most,
even though you are his daughter.

146
00:05:45,428 --> 00:05:47,805
But I suspect him.

147
00:05:47,806 --> 00:05:50,057
He said he dragged the body.

148
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:52,268
- Right? In his own words…
- Exactly.

149
00:05:52,269 --> 00:05:54,270
He basically confessed.

150
00:05:54,271 --> 00:05:57,773
It makes no sense
that he dragged the body all that way.

151
00:05:57,774 --> 00:06:02,111
He knows the layout of the house
better than anyone.

152
00:06:02,112 --> 00:06:03,904
The Traveler would not know that well.

153
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:05,030
He slipped up.

154
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:07,449
Yes, he confessed by accident.

155
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:09,159
A dead body isn't easy to drag around.

156
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:10,369
Yes, you're right.

157
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:11,538
I think you are right.

158
00:06:12,122 --> 00:06:13,330
Let's live happily together.

159
00:06:13,331 --> 00:06:15,374
Yes. This is your father's problem.

160
00:06:15,375 --> 00:06:17,877
I consider my relationship with you

161
00:06:17,878 --> 00:06:21,255
an honor for a family
that is disregarded like mine.

162
00:06:21,256 --> 00:06:22,756
I think of it as an honor.

163
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,509
So, where should we run away to?

164
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:26,302
Let us go to Muju.

165
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:27,887
RIGHT UP MY ALLEY

166
00:06:27,888 --> 00:06:30,097
- Muju Gucheong-dong Valley?
- Yes. Let us go to Muju.

167
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:32,308
- It is famous for its view.
- Though it's a bit far…

168
00:06:32,309 --> 00:06:34,518
Let's get going, Lady.
Do you want a piggyback?

169
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:36,103
Sure. Can you manage?

170
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:38,273
Yes. Get on. Let us go.

171
00:06:39,024 --> 00:06:40,984
[straining, grunting]

172
00:06:41,610 --> 00:06:43,403
[both laugh]

173
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,613
I have a question.

174
00:06:45,614 --> 00:06:48,490
The note we saw earlier said
whoever killed Yun Igyeong

175
00:06:48,491 --> 00:06:50,784
<i>would be appointed to office.</i>

176
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,703
Did you write that,
Grand Prince Hwiryeong?

177
00:06:52,704 --> 00:06:53,788
- Me?
- Yes.

178
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,041
Why would I?

179
00:06:57,167 --> 00:06:58,751
[Musoe] You have the authority…

180
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:00,794
- Grand Prince Hwiryeong?
-…to appoint someone.

181
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:02,421
You're in a high enough position.

182
00:07:02,422 --> 00:07:04,090
- He's Grand Prince Hwiryeong?
- Yes.

183
00:07:04,591 --> 00:07:06,592
I'm Grand Prince Hwiryeong.

184
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:07,677
[both] Your Highness.

185
00:07:08,303 --> 00:07:09,386
Do you understand now?

186
00:07:09,387 --> 00:07:10,597
HE ONLY TOLD YUN SUYEON
AND MUSOE

187
00:07:13,183 --> 00:07:14,643
- How is that possible?
- [Musoe chuckles]

188
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:17,102
- The truth is--
- I'm supposed to know the grand prince.

189
00:07:17,103 --> 00:07:20,147
[Igyeong] <i>I was exiled for writing
a petition to the King,</i>

190
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:23,192
<i>and it was the Grand Prince Hwiryeong
who ordered me to do it.</i>

191
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:24,818
<i>We know each other,</i>

192
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:26,737
<i>so he can't be Grand Prince Hwiryeong.</i>

193
00:07:26,738 --> 00:07:27,781
CAN'T BE THE SAME PERSON?

194
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:29,741
Is there a new grand prince?

195
00:07:30,742 --> 00:07:32,661
- Did his role change? Is he retired?
- The truth is,

196
00:07:33,244 --> 00:07:34,496
Grand Prince Hwiryeong is actually…

197
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:38,332
WHO IS GRAND PRINCE HWIRYEONG?

198
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:41,543
…he is the one who told me,
"Yun Igyeong is plotting treason,

199
00:07:41,544 --> 00:07:44,005
so he should be
removed from office and exiled."

200
00:07:44,506 --> 00:07:46,675
The grand prince is actually
my younger brother.

201
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:49,259
WHAT?

202
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,511
[gasps, chuckles]

203
00:07:50,512 --> 00:07:52,262
So, you are the King? Your Majesty?

204
00:07:52,263 --> 00:07:53,264
I am

205
00:07:54,224 --> 00:07:55,475
the ruler of this nation.

206
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:57,851
What the heck?

207
00:07:57,852 --> 00:08:00,146
WHY DO YOU KEEP CHANGING?

208
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:02,232
The truth is,

209
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:05,234
I am the king of this nation.

210
00:08:05,235 --> 00:08:06,695
You've come in person?

211
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:08,445
That is right.

212
00:08:08,446 --> 00:08:11,323
I have the face of a king.

213
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:14,159
I didn't mention this earlier,

214
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:18,331
but I am playing King Sejong in a musical,
and I've played a king on another show.

215
00:08:18,790 --> 00:08:20,749
IS THE TRAVELER REALLY THE KING?

216
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:21,959
[sighs]

217
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:23,043
ROUND 3 CARD CLUES

218
00:08:23,044 --> 00:08:24,545
IGYEONG'S DIARY, HUNTER'S WARNING,
INNKEEPER'S STATEMENT

219
00:08:24,546 --> 00:08:25,547
KITCHEN CEILING,
GRAND PRINCE'S LETTER

220
00:08:26,172 --> 00:08:27,256
ROUND 4

221
00:08:27,257 --> 00:08:29,384
Oh, goodness.
I had better take one from Musoe.

222
00:08:29,801 --> 00:08:31,970
YUN SUYEON TAKES
A CARD FROM MUSOE

223
00:08:32,345 --> 00:08:33,930
BOKGIL TAKES A CARD
FROM YUN IGYEONG

224
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:36,682
MUSOE TAKES ONE FROM YUN SUYEON

225
00:08:36,683 --> 00:08:37,934
THE TRAVELER TAKES ONE
FROM MUSOE

226
00:08:38,518 --> 00:08:39,644
YUN IGYEONG TAKES ONE
FROM YUN SUYEON

227
00:08:40,228 --> 00:08:41,229
[Suyeon] I want this one.

228
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:44,231
- It is a bit heavy.
- [Bokgil] Let's lift it together.

229
00:08:44,232 --> 00:08:45,942
There's also this.

230
00:08:46,651 --> 00:08:49,069
OBJECT CLUES COLLECTED

231
00:08:49,070 --> 00:08:51,281
This contains a very telling clue.

232
00:08:51,823 --> 00:08:54,074
This belongs to my dad.

233
00:08:54,075 --> 00:08:56,326
Why are you reading my diary?

234
00:08:56,327 --> 00:08:59,622
[Suyeon] "Grand Prince Hwiryeong told me
to submit a petition to the King."

235
00:09:00,206 --> 00:09:01,999
"I also oppose the recent tax reform,

236
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:06,587
so I put my heart
into writing the petition."

237
00:09:06,588 --> 00:09:10,132
"Grand Prince Hwiryeong is truly
a prince who cares for the people."

238
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:12,718
The diary is suggesting

239
00:09:12,719 --> 00:09:15,680
that Grand Prince Hwiryeong
is a good person, right?

240
00:09:16,556 --> 00:09:17,639
[Suyeon] Yes.

241
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:18,724
YUN IGYEONG TRUSTED
THE GRAND PRINCE

242
00:09:18,725 --> 00:09:20,642
Before we discuss this,

243
00:09:20,643 --> 00:09:23,021
Grand Prince Hwiryeong
isn't who he said he was.

244
00:09:24,439 --> 00:09:26,273
Then he's the killer!

245
00:09:26,274 --> 00:09:27,775
- He isn't the killer.
- Actually,

246
00:09:27,776 --> 00:09:28,859
he is our nation's--

247
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:30,319
[Musoe] You're in real trouble now,
Suyeon.

248
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,403
He is our nation's king.

249
00:09:31,404 --> 00:09:34,531
- I am the King of Joseon.
- [gasps]

250
00:09:34,532 --> 00:09:37,242
- [others laughing]
- Forgive me, Your Majesty!

251
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:39,579
[♪ dramatic music playing]

252
00:09:42,749 --> 00:09:43,832
KING

253
00:09:43,833 --> 00:09:46,669
RULER OF JOSEON, THE PERSON
WHO SENT YUN IGYEONG INTO EXILE

254
00:09:47,295 --> 00:09:49,296
[contestants] Your Majesty!

255
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:50,380
[Bokgil] He really is the King.

256
00:09:50,381 --> 00:09:52,925
- All who doubted me, bow your heads!
- Your Majesty.

257
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:55,385
- His Majesty has a lot of spare time.
- [Suyeon] I'm honestly amazed

258
00:09:55,386 --> 00:09:56,805
that the King wanders around alone.

259
00:09:57,305 --> 00:09:58,722
More like a madman than a king.

260
00:09:58,723 --> 00:10:00,307
HOW INSOLENT

261
00:10:00,308 --> 00:10:01,975
Why did you come here yourself,
Your Majesty?

262
00:10:01,976 --> 00:10:05,104
[King] <i>Despite what it says on here,</i>

263
00:10:05,105 --> 00:10:07,773
<i>the one who sent Yun Igyeong into exile
was actually</i>

264
00:10:07,774 --> 00:10:08,942
<i>the grand prince.</i>

265
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:12,487
GRAND PRINCE HWIRYEONG PITTED
THE KING AGAINST HIS MINISTERS

266
00:10:13,071 --> 00:10:15,740
A PLOT WAS HATCHED
AMIDST THE CHAOS

267
00:10:16,699 --> 00:10:19,744
BUT THE KING CAUGHT ON
AND WENT INTO HIDING

268
00:10:20,912 --> 00:10:25,290
HE TRACKED DOWN YUN IGYEONG IN EXILE
TO FIND OUT THE TRUTH FROM HIM

269
00:10:25,291 --> 00:10:28,794
So I was tricked
by Grand Prince Hwiryeong?

270
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:30,045
- You were mistaken.
- I trusted him.

271
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:31,213
ALLEGIANCE

272
00:10:31,214 --> 00:10:33,715
POLITICAL SCAPEGOAT

273
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:36,844
- [Suyeon] Musoe.
- I found another knife, goodness.

274
00:10:36,845 --> 00:10:38,554
Why are there so many knives?

275
00:10:38,555 --> 00:10:41,265
[Bokgil] <i>It was under a laundry stone.</i>

276
00:10:41,266 --> 00:10:42,809
Then it must be Musoe's.

277
00:10:43,434 --> 00:10:45,727
- It is my kitchen knife…
- [Bokgil] Hey!

278
00:10:45,728 --> 00:10:49,314
…but because I am so dainty,
I cut my hand…

279
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:51,150
- [Bokgil] It's your blood?
- Yes.

280
00:10:51,151 --> 00:10:52,568
- Not the murder weapon?
- At the time,

281
00:10:52,569 --> 00:10:54,486
- I had nowhere to wipe it.
- But there's blood here too.

282
00:10:54,487 --> 00:10:56,238
Listen, everyone.

283
00:10:56,239 --> 00:10:59,032
There was a note
in Musoe's recipe book that said,

284
00:10:59,033 --> 00:11:00,201
"Am I…

285
00:11:01,953 --> 00:11:03,704
my master's child?"

286
00:11:03,705 --> 00:11:05,038
Hmm?

287
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:06,498
Musoe?

288
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:07,749
- Master? Yun Igyeong?
- Musoe?

289
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,001
From Musoe's recipe book.

290
00:11:09,002 --> 00:11:10,044
[Suyeon] Ah…

291
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:14,090
- [Suyeon] But--
- Oh!

292
00:11:15,258 --> 00:11:18,343
They were switched!

293
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:19,387
The switched kids.

294
00:11:20,096 --> 00:11:22,472
So my daughter was…

295
00:11:22,473 --> 00:11:24,434
My real daughter is Musoe.

296
00:11:25,643 --> 00:11:28,228
Yun Suyeon was from a different family

297
00:11:28,229 --> 00:11:31,982
and the victim is her actual father.

298
00:11:31,983 --> 00:11:34,026
<i>But they were switched as kids,</i>

299
00:11:34,027 --> 00:11:36,195
- <i>so he came to find his real daughter.</i>
- [Musoe] <i>He sought her out.</i>

300
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:37,905
Musoe wasn't just mistaken?

301
00:11:37,906 --> 00:11:40,199
I overheard someone say

302
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:42,869
that I am Lord Yun's real daughter.

303
00:11:43,453 --> 00:11:46,915
MUSOE HEARD TALK IN THE MARKET
ABOUT YUN SUYEON'S REAL DAD

304
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:49,918
MUSOE WAS BORN RICH
BUT GREW UP POOR

305
00:11:50,501 --> 00:11:54,923
HER LIFE WAS STOLEN FROM HER,
SO SHE DECIDED TO TAKE REVENGE

306
00:11:55,215 --> 00:11:56,882
FATHER-DAUGHTER
YUN IGYEONG, YUN SUYEON

307
00:11:56,883 --> 00:11:58,675
FATHER-DAUGHTER
YUN IGYEONG, MUSOE

308
00:11:58,676 --> 00:12:01,220
They traded lives.

309
00:12:01,221 --> 00:12:03,889
- So she's not a lady, just a slave?
- Yes.

310
00:12:03,890 --> 00:12:06,141
- You two are a good match.
- You're a nobody.

311
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:07,602
- Birds of a feather.
- Lady, my foot.

312
00:12:08,186 --> 00:12:09,770
- We're a match made in heaven.
- [laughing]

313
00:12:09,771 --> 00:12:10,979
No!

314
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:12,064
IN DENIAL

315
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:14,149
You heard it. You two were switched.

316
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:15,484
- You and Musoe.
- No, I wasn't.

317
00:12:15,485 --> 00:12:17,444
You don't have the facial features

318
00:12:17,445 --> 00:12:18,695
of a noble lady.

319
00:12:18,696 --> 00:12:20,949
OH, MAN

320
00:12:21,449 --> 00:12:25,953
THE SLAVE COUPLE
OF EQUAL SOCIAL STATUS

321
00:12:25,954 --> 00:12:27,037
[Igyeong] <i>If the victim</i>

322
00:12:27,038 --> 00:12:29,331
was revealed to be her father,

323
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:31,416
who had the most to lose?

324
00:12:31,417 --> 00:12:34,002
She did. Yun Suyeon.

325
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:35,796
She just wrinkled her nose.

326
00:12:35,797 --> 00:12:38,298
That's a tell when you're guilty.

327
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:39,758
I have rhinitis…

328
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:41,426
- Your Majesty.
- [Igyeong] And the victim knew

329
00:12:41,427 --> 00:12:44,805
Yun Suyeon was his daughter,

330
00:12:44,806 --> 00:12:47,599
so she could approach him
without him suspecting her.

331
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,476
When he had his guard down,

332
00:12:49,477 --> 00:12:50,645
she took the silver dagger and…

333
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:53,522
DID SUYEON STAB HER REAL FATHER?

334
00:12:53,523 --> 00:12:54,773
That's my guess.

335
00:12:54,774 --> 00:12:57,276
But we heard the audio earlier,

336
00:12:57,277 --> 00:13:00,696
a silver dagger could never
make that kind of sound.

337
00:13:00,697 --> 00:13:02,114
The first blade sound was--

338
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:04,283
The first sound was me.

339
00:13:04,284 --> 00:13:07,202
ME?

340
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:08,662
In the dark of the night

341
00:13:08,663 --> 00:13:11,039
I heard a noise, so I went out
and something whipped past me,

342
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,958
so I swung my sword as a reflex.

343
00:13:12,959 --> 00:13:15,377
It didn't feel like I struck anyone.

344
00:13:15,378 --> 00:13:17,087
Why did you do such a scary thing?

345
00:13:17,088 --> 00:13:18,171
In the dead of night.

346
00:13:18,172 --> 00:13:19,589
- What a weird king.
- Right?

347
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:21,049
This is why our nation is in ruin!

348
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:23,802
It could have been an assassin

349
00:13:23,803 --> 00:13:26,096
sent by Grand Prince Hwiryeong
to take my life.

350
00:13:26,097 --> 00:13:28,349
- So that's why--
- Oh, you thought it was an assassin?

351
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:36,023
DID HE FEAR ASSASSINATION
EVERY NIGHT?

352
00:13:36,024 --> 00:13:39,526
I have a question for Musoe.

353
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:42,904
There is a trail of blood
coming out from the kitchen.

354
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:47,200
So I want to know why
Musoe left the kitchen bleeding

355
00:13:47,201 --> 00:13:49,579
and the trail overlaps here.

356
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:53,707
I told you I knew you planned
to run away in the night,

357
00:13:53,708 --> 00:13:55,292
so I was out and about at that time.

358
00:13:55,293 --> 00:13:57,503
The truth is that I was jealous of you

359
00:13:58,004 --> 00:13:59,588
since I'm Lord Yun's real daughter,

360
00:13:59,589 --> 00:14:01,590
and now you even stole Bokgil away.

361
00:14:01,591 --> 00:14:03,842
- So I wanted to kill you.
- [Bokgil] Huh?

362
00:14:03,843 --> 00:14:05,927
[Musoe] I even held
the kitchen knife to do it.

363
00:14:05,928 --> 00:14:07,471
- But why is it bloody?
- Why is there blood?

364
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:08,889
- I never got stabbed.
- [Musoe] But then,

365
00:14:08,890 --> 00:14:10,349
I went to the kitchen to get the knife,

366
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:12,268
but someone was in there.

367
00:14:13,061 --> 00:14:14,603
<i>I wasn't sure who it was,</i>

368
00:14:14,604 --> 00:14:17,147
<i>but I also felt I was in danger,
so I swung the knife.</i>

369
00:14:17,148 --> 00:14:19,900
So the first blade sound was me.

370
00:14:19,901 --> 00:14:21,193
The one not followed by screams.

371
00:14:21,194 --> 00:14:22,195
What?

372
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:24,154
[Musoe] And then,

373
00:14:24,155 --> 00:14:26,615
as I was running away, I shook them off,

374
00:14:26,616 --> 00:14:28,784
<i>banged my head, and briefly blacked out</i>

375
00:14:28,785 --> 00:14:30,160
<i>for about 30 minutes.</i>

376
00:14:30,161 --> 00:14:31,746
So there are two people who swung a blade?

377
00:14:33,081 --> 00:14:36,625
WERE THOSE TWO PEOPLE
MUSOE AND THE TRAVELER?

378
00:14:36,626 --> 00:14:39,586
Did you not see their face in the dark?

379
00:14:39,587 --> 00:14:41,172
No, I could not see their face.

380
00:14:41,756 --> 00:14:43,006
It was too dark.

381
00:14:43,007 --> 00:14:45,133
I am not even sure if I struck them.

382
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:47,260
You said you did the same thing,
Your Majesty.

383
00:14:47,261 --> 00:14:48,595
You swung your sword.

384
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:49,930
Yes, I swung it.

385
00:14:49,931 --> 00:14:52,933
Based on the time and the route,
I swung my knife first.

386
00:14:52,934 --> 00:14:54,267
THE SECOND SWINGER
IS THE KILLER?

387
00:14:54,268 --> 00:14:56,603
So I find you very suspicious,
Your Majesty.

388
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:59,065
Well, that narrows it down.

389
00:14:59,607 --> 00:15:01,274
Your daughter, Suyeon,

390
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:04,444
was actually switched as a child.

391
00:15:04,445 --> 00:15:05,987
All the evidence is

392
00:15:05,988 --> 00:15:07,073
<i>a silver dagger,</i>

393
00:15:07,824 --> 00:15:08,825
<i>a sword,</i>

394
00:15:09,659 --> 00:15:10,660
<i>and a kitchen knife.</i>

395
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:13,287
Which of those three
had the biggest motive?

396
00:15:13,913 --> 00:15:15,206
I have already made my mind up.

397
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:16,791
<i>It is Suyeon.</i>

398
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:20,710
MEANWHILE IN THE EVIDENCE ZONE

399
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:23,922
SUYEON OPENS A CHEST

400
00:15:23,923 --> 00:15:25,258
Number five, please.

401
00:15:26,134 --> 00:15:27,592
- What's that?
- There's no evidence.

402
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:30,095
- There's something dangling.
- It's a key!

403
00:15:30,096 --> 00:15:31,597
Am I the only one who can use this key?

404
00:15:32,181 --> 00:15:33,473
Yippee!

405
00:15:33,474 --> 00:15:35,225
HIDDEN CLUE

406
00:15:35,226 --> 00:15:37,644
THE KEY FROM THE SCROLL
CAN BE USED TO OPEN A CHEST

407
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:40,273
THE PLAYER WHO OPENS IT IS
FREE TO SHARE OR HIDE THE CLUE

408
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,528
What is this?

409
00:15:47,780 --> 00:15:48,990
What is it?

410
00:15:52,451 --> 00:15:54,370
The King's garment.

411
00:15:58,666 --> 00:15:59,667
[gasps]

412
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:03,044
[whispering] He killed the King!

413
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:05,088
Then he changed into his robes.

414
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:06,590
That bastard!

415
00:16:06,591 --> 00:16:07,674
<i>I got chills.</i>

416
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:10,302
The person who calls himself the King

417
00:16:10,303 --> 00:16:11,887
killed the actual King

418
00:16:11,888 --> 00:16:13,805
and put on the King's robes.

419
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:15,182
THE TRAVELER IS NOT THE KING?

420
00:16:15,183 --> 00:16:16,266
ROUND 4 CARD CLUES

421
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:17,392
APOTHECARY NOTE,
RECORD OF OFFICIAL SERVICE

422
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:18,852
BOKGIL'S NOTE, MUSOE'S RECIPE
BOOK, VILLAGER'S STATEMENT

423
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:21,189
[host] <i>It is the fifth and final round.</i>

424
00:16:21,480 --> 00:16:22,564
ROUND 5 SHARED CLUE
AUTOPSY REPORT

425
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:23,690
[Igyeong] <i>An autopsy report.</i>

426
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:27,152
"Judging by the straight spear wound,

427
00:16:27,153 --> 00:16:29,279
the victim was struck while moving

428
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:31,990
with a single preemptive strike
by someone highly skilled."

429
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:34,367
"The wound shows the blade never wavered."

430
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:35,827
An unwavering blade.

431
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:37,370
[Bokgil] It must be a sword.

432
00:16:37,371 --> 00:16:38,455
- [Suyeon] But--
- This--

433
00:16:38,456 --> 00:16:39,915
Can we use this right now?

434
00:16:39,916 --> 00:16:40,917
The arm…

435
00:16:41,876 --> 00:16:43,585
Here you go. It is number three.

436
00:16:43,586 --> 00:16:45,129
- Three?
- Yes, three.

437
00:16:47,715 --> 00:16:50,050
SCROLL CLUE NO. 3
YUN SUYEON'S PORTRAIT

438
00:16:50,051 --> 00:16:52,678
There's a blade wound on her neck

439
00:16:53,554 --> 00:16:54,555
and a mark on her hand.

440
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:56,807
A BLADE WOUND
ON YUN SUYEON'S NECK

441
00:16:57,350 --> 00:16:59,560
AND A BLUE MARK
ON THE BACK OF HER HAND

442
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:02,021
Lord Yun.

443
00:17:02,521 --> 00:17:04,898
- You need to come and see this.
- [Suyeon] I'd better use mine too.

444
00:17:04,899 --> 00:17:06,900
RUSHING OVER

445
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:09,445
- [Musoe] That is Yun Suyeon's portrait.
- [Bokgil] Oh.

446
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,988
[Musoe] There's a blade wound on her neck

447
00:17:11,989 --> 00:17:13,823
and a mark on her hand.

448
00:17:13,824 --> 00:17:15,575
She must've done it to get out
of leaving with Bokgil.

449
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:17,202
- She tried to end her own life?
- Yes.

450
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:19,621
- To avoid getting caught.
- That's the blood on the silver dagger.

451
00:17:19,622 --> 00:17:21,040
The murder victim

452
00:17:21,666 --> 00:17:23,625
is Yun Suyeon's father,

453
00:17:23,626 --> 00:17:24,751
her biological dad.

454
00:17:24,752 --> 00:17:26,753
But she wasn't trying to kill him.

455
00:17:26,754 --> 00:17:28,797
- She tried to off herself.
- She tried to take her own life.

456
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:29,881
SUYEON ATTEMPTED TO DIE

457
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:32,634
She would rather die than live as a slave.

458
00:17:32,635 --> 00:17:33,843
That's why she did it.

459
00:17:33,844 --> 00:17:34,970
<i>The revealed portrait</i>

460
00:17:34,971 --> 00:17:36,972
showed a blade wound on her neck.

461
00:17:36,973 --> 00:17:39,391
I thought it was the victim's blood
on the silver dagger,

462
00:17:39,392 --> 00:17:40,809
<i>but it wasn't.</i>

463
00:17:40,810 --> 00:17:42,102
<i>I am sure that it was</i>

464
00:17:42,103 --> 00:17:43,938
her own blood from trying
to take her own life.

465
00:17:44,522 --> 00:17:46,273
I suspected she was the killer at first,

466
00:17:46,274 --> 00:17:49,276
but the evidence shows that
she harmed herself,

467
00:17:49,277 --> 00:17:50,610
so I don't suspect her anymore.

468
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:52,571
I'll use mine too.

469
00:17:52,572 --> 00:17:54,447
[sighs] My head hurts.

470
00:17:54,448 --> 00:17:55,615
What's this?

471
00:17:55,616 --> 00:17:58,451
SCROLL CLUE NO. 5
ASSASSIN WARNING NOTICE

472
00:17:58,452 --> 00:17:59,912
That assassin is wearing glasses.

473
00:18:00,997 --> 00:18:02,581
- Bokgil?
- [Suyeon] Hmm…

474
00:18:02,582 --> 00:18:03,665
[gasps]

475
00:18:03,666 --> 00:18:05,792
It's him!

476
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:07,544
- [Musoe] You're right!
- [Suyeon] It's Bokgil!

477
00:18:07,545 --> 00:18:09,045
THE ASSASSIN LOOKS
JUST LIKE BOKGIL

478
00:18:09,046 --> 00:18:10,171
[Bokgil chuckles]

479
00:18:10,172 --> 00:18:12,048
You're suddenly turning on me like this?

480
00:18:12,049 --> 00:18:14,426
But seeing those glasses,
it really does look like you.

481
00:18:14,427 --> 00:18:17,221
[Igyeong] He also has
a thick head of hair like you.

482
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:19,347
- I think it's him.
- He's an assassin.

483
00:18:19,348 --> 00:18:21,016
- Bokgil's an assassin.
- Suddenly?

484
00:18:21,017 --> 00:18:24,394
[Musoe] Bokgil seems like an assassin

485
00:18:24,395 --> 00:18:26,062
who was acting under orders.

486
00:18:26,063 --> 00:18:28,024
[Bokgil] I'm an impressive guy like that?

487
00:18:28,983 --> 00:18:31,610
Grand Prince Hwiryeong and the King

488
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:34,487
seem to have been
engaged in a political conflict

489
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:35,989
that forms the backdrop.

490
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:39,326
<i>And Lord Yun got caught
in the middle of it.</i>

491
00:18:39,327 --> 00:18:43,414
<i>And I think Bokgil is an assassin
working under Lord Yun.</i>

492
00:18:43,956 --> 00:18:47,792
WHO HIRED BOKGIL AS AN ASSASSIN?

493
00:18:47,793 --> 00:18:50,670
Bokgil is on His Majesty's side

494
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:53,173
or one of Grand Prince Hwiryeong's men.

495
00:18:53,174 --> 00:18:55,842
Whether he was sent to protect Lord Yun

496
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:58,345
or hired to kill someone,

497
00:18:58,346 --> 00:19:01,306
I think that's the gist of his role.

498
00:19:01,307 --> 00:19:02,724
It is true

499
00:19:02,725 --> 00:19:04,142
that I am here under the order

500
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:05,226
of the grand prince.

501
00:19:05,227 --> 00:19:06,645
- [Musoe] Grand Prince Hwiryeong?
- Yes.

502
00:19:06,646 --> 00:19:07,937
Grand Prince Hwiryeong sent you.

503
00:19:07,938 --> 00:19:09,272
WAS HE HIRED TO ACT AS A SLAVE?

504
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:11,358
Why did you try to run away with Suyeon?

505
00:19:11,359 --> 00:19:14,402
Because I love Lady Suyeon.

506
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:17,489
- You fell in love on the job?
- [Suyeon, Bokgil] Yes.

507
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:19,908
But I had nothing to do with the murder.

508
00:19:19,909 --> 00:19:21,951
I was planning to run away.

509
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:23,953
Why would I do this and foil my own plans?

510
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:25,955
You said were ordered
by Grand Prince Hwiryeong.

511
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:27,916
- Yes, well--
- [Musoe] What were his orders?

512
00:19:27,917 --> 00:19:29,959
- To report back his every move.
- Lord Yun?

513
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:31,169
Yes, on Lord Yun.

514
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:35,174
Was it positive surveillance
for his protection?

515
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:37,885
Who are you to interrogate me?

516
00:19:41,055 --> 00:19:42,972
[Bokgil] That's all I have to say.

517
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:46,476
But keeping watch is
usually a negative thing.

518
00:19:46,477 --> 00:19:48,186
A government office was promised

519
00:19:48,187 --> 00:19:51,232
to the one who killed Lord Yun
and that person is you, right?

520
00:19:51,899 --> 00:19:54,193
GRAND PRINCE HWIRYEONG
CAUGHT ON TO THE KING'S PLANS

521
00:19:54,443 --> 00:19:56,236
BOKGIL WAS ORDERED
TO ASSASSINATE LORD YUN

522
00:19:56,237 --> 00:19:57,487
[Bokgil] <i>I did consider it</i>

523
00:19:57,488 --> 00:19:59,364
by making a deadly poison

524
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:01,157
but I didn't even think to use a blade.

525
00:20:01,158 --> 00:20:04,078
I've never used a sword before.
I can't even cut an apple.

526
00:20:04,954 --> 00:20:06,121
Bokgil!

527
00:20:06,122 --> 00:20:07,832
AT THE TIME
THEY AGREED TO RUN AWAY

528
00:20:08,290 --> 00:20:11,794
BOKGIL CHOSE AMBITION OVER LOVE

529
00:20:12,294 --> 00:20:16,840
DID YUN SUYEON TRY TO END HERSELF
BECAUSE SHE FELT ABANDONED?

530
00:20:16,841 --> 00:20:19,217
LOST IN THOUGHT

531
00:20:19,218 --> 00:20:21,428
Lord Yun, why are you suddenly

532
00:20:21,429 --> 00:20:22,887
so quiet?

533
00:20:22,888 --> 00:20:25,765
- I kept suspecting Yun Suyeon…
- Right.

534
00:20:25,766 --> 00:20:27,393
…but now I think you are the culprit.

535
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:30,938
The figure in the clue we just saw
was wearing glasses, after all.

536
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:34,524
[King] Bokgil wanted to rise up
through society.

537
00:20:34,525 --> 00:20:35,608
[chuckles]

538
00:20:35,609 --> 00:20:38,278
He really loved Yun Suyeon,

539
00:20:38,279 --> 00:20:41,156
so he wanted to run away with her
and leave his past behind.

540
00:20:41,157 --> 00:20:44,534
But if Suyeon's real father
revealed her identity,

541
00:20:44,535 --> 00:20:46,202
<i>it would mess everything up.</i>

542
00:20:46,203 --> 00:20:48,163
<i>So putting aside
his assignment to kill me,</i>

543
00:20:48,164 --> 00:20:50,165
<i>I think he killed
Yun Suyeon's real father.</i>

544
00:20:50,166 --> 00:20:53,501
If it is true that Bokgil is an assassin,

545
00:20:53,502 --> 00:20:55,962
<i>it says the victim was moving,
but the strike was precise.</i>

546
00:20:55,963 --> 00:21:00,383
It's a kind of feat
that a dainty woman like Yun Suyeon

547
00:21:00,384 --> 00:21:03,970
couldn't easily pull off.

548
00:21:03,971 --> 00:21:06,473
I think the assassin killed the victim

549
00:21:06,474 --> 00:21:08,558
with the single strike of a blade,

550
00:21:08,559 --> 00:21:11,644
then wiped the blood off
with the handkerchief we saw earlier.

551
00:21:11,645 --> 00:21:13,480
I thought it was Yun Suyeon but--

552
00:21:13,481 --> 00:21:15,398
- I am not the killer.
- No, you're not.

553
00:21:15,399 --> 00:21:16,816
I think Yun Suyeon

554
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:18,359
didn't want to go back to being a slave,

555
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:21,488
<i>so she tried to take her own life
after seeing her real father.</i>

556
00:21:21,489 --> 00:21:23,324
I think it's one of two people.

557
00:21:24,116 --> 00:21:25,450
These two.

558
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:27,327
- [Musoe] I agree.
- [Suyeon] It was either Bokgil

559
00:21:27,328 --> 00:21:29,246
or the man who claims to be the King.

560
00:21:29,872 --> 00:21:31,456
Here's what I find suspicious.

561
00:21:31,457 --> 00:21:33,793
I don't believe he is the King,
and here's why.

562
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:35,668
This is

563
00:21:35,669 --> 00:21:37,879
the garment worn

564
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:39,172
beneath a king's robes.

565
00:21:39,173 --> 00:21:41,342
Are you wearing one right now?

566
00:21:41,967 --> 00:21:43,593
It's under this robe.

567
00:21:43,594 --> 00:21:45,429
And it is marked precisely

568
00:21:45,930 --> 00:21:46,931
as the King's.

569
00:21:47,765 --> 00:21:49,974
The King is dead.

570
00:21:49,975 --> 00:21:51,559
The King has died.

571
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:54,020
That person sitting there
in the King's robes

572
00:21:54,021 --> 00:21:55,688
cannot be His Majesty.

573
00:21:55,689 --> 00:21:57,106
WHAT IS THE TRAVELER'S IDENTITY?

574
00:21:57,107 --> 00:21:59,234
I'm Grand Prince Hwiryeong.

575
00:21:59,235 --> 00:22:00,443
Grand Prince Hwiryeong?

576
00:22:00,444 --> 00:22:02,320
- I am the King of Joseon.
- [Suyeon gasps]

577
00:22:02,321 --> 00:22:03,906
THE KING OF JOSEON?

578
00:22:04,573 --> 00:22:08,409
OR AN ASSASSIN?

579
00:22:08,410 --> 00:22:10,453
Sorry, but can I say something?

580
00:22:10,454 --> 00:22:11,872
The King isn't dead.

581
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:14,166
The King is the killer.

582
00:22:14,750 --> 00:22:17,126
He took off his royal robe,
and in just his undergarments,

583
00:22:17,127 --> 00:22:18,878
he killed the victim
and the blood splattered.

584
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:20,922
That is why the card says "king."

585
00:22:20,923 --> 00:22:23,508
He got splattered from killing the victim?

586
00:22:23,509 --> 00:22:24,843
The King is the killer?

587
00:22:24,844 --> 00:22:27,136
Yes, His Majesty is the killer.

588
00:22:27,137 --> 00:22:29,639
- It's a bit--
- But that doesn't make any sense

589
00:22:29,640 --> 00:22:32,350
because the King can order
anyone to be executed.

590
00:22:32,351 --> 00:22:33,726
Why go to this trouble at night

591
00:22:33,727 --> 00:22:36,063
- to kill someone?
- I came to protect Yun Igyeong.

592
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:38,815
- He isn't the King.
- People are disposable to him.

593
00:22:38,816 --> 00:22:40,316
[Bokgil] You're really the King?

594
00:22:40,317 --> 00:22:41,442
IS HE REALLY THE KING?

595
00:22:41,443 --> 00:22:42,527
FRUSTRATED

596
00:22:42,528 --> 00:22:44,612
If the King was going to kill someone…

597
00:22:44,613 --> 00:22:46,364
- This is so hard!
-…he'd sentence them to execution.

598
00:22:46,365 --> 00:22:47,448
[King] Explain to me

599
00:22:47,449 --> 00:22:49,742
- what reason I had to kill the victim.
- [Bokgil] Why go out of his way--

600
00:22:49,743 --> 00:22:52,495
- If the King is guilty…
- Why would I do it?

601
00:22:52,496 --> 00:22:53,580
…what would be his motive?

602
00:22:53,581 --> 00:22:55,164
Lord Yun was the King's closest aide,

603
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:57,625
so maybe the King came to kill him.

604
00:22:57,626 --> 00:23:00,461
Then I would have killed Lord Yun.

605
00:23:00,462 --> 00:23:02,630
- Why kill that other person?
- That's a good question.

606
00:23:02,631 --> 00:23:04,924
- [Musoe] Grand Prince Hwiryeong--
- Or maybe,

607
00:23:04,925 --> 00:23:05,968
it was you

608
00:23:06,468 --> 00:23:07,469
getting revenge.

609
00:23:08,554 --> 00:23:10,555
REVENGE?

610
00:23:10,556 --> 00:23:12,515
Yeah, it could be you!
Why are you acting innocent?

611
00:23:12,516 --> 00:23:15,059
Your life was ruined, after all.

612
00:23:15,060 --> 00:23:18,938
"I was born as the daughter
of a fancy household,

613
00:23:18,939 --> 00:23:21,983
but I grew up as a slave
for 20 or so years because of you."

614
00:23:21,984 --> 00:23:24,193
It is true I was jealous,

615
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:25,945
but then I would have killed Lady Yun.

616
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:28,948
Not if you put the blame

617
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:31,619
- on the person who switched you.
- I held them responsible.

618
00:23:32,411 --> 00:23:35,038
Honestly, I am so confused.

619
00:23:35,039 --> 00:23:37,540
I thought I had everything
figured out more or less,

620
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:40,501
but the most important question
of why he was killed is still a mystery.

621
00:23:40,502 --> 00:23:43,422
I will base my vote
on the highest probability.

622
00:23:44,048 --> 00:23:46,090
[chuckles]
Make your closing argument first.

623
00:23:46,091 --> 00:23:48,676
This murder case honestly
has nothing to do with me.

624
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:51,429
I hope you will vote
for someone who is capable

625
00:23:51,430 --> 00:23:53,848
of skillfully handling a blade.

626
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:55,767
It makes no sense for me to be the killer.

627
00:23:55,768 --> 00:23:58,436
I was just trying to run away with Bokgil.

628
00:23:58,437 --> 00:24:01,523
I am only guilty of loving Bokgil!

629
00:24:02,816 --> 00:24:04,108
It is the same for me.

630
00:24:04,109 --> 00:24:05,568
We are a package deal.

631
00:24:05,569 --> 00:24:07,320
"Package deal."

632
00:24:07,321 --> 00:24:09,447
My only crime is falling in love.

633
00:24:09,448 --> 00:24:12,241
If we had just run away
30 minutes earlier,

634
00:24:12,242 --> 00:24:14,118
we would never have
even known about the murder.

635
00:24:14,119 --> 00:24:15,621
I am…

636
00:24:16,497 --> 00:24:17,665
a virtuous king.

637
00:24:18,916 --> 00:24:20,083
For the sake of my nation…

638
00:24:20,084 --> 00:24:21,793
- He's so suspicious.
-…I really…

639
00:24:21,794 --> 00:24:23,336
I do not even know who the victim is

640
00:24:23,337 --> 00:24:24,712
or why they were killed.

641
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:27,507
The first blade swing was me,

642
00:24:27,508 --> 00:24:30,510
but as you heard on the audio clip,

643
00:24:30,511 --> 00:24:32,261
no one screamed after the first swing.

644
00:24:32,262 --> 00:24:34,973
We only heard a scream
after the second swing of a blade.

645
00:24:34,974 --> 00:24:38,226
And I urge you to consider
that conclusive piece of evidence.

646
00:24:38,227 --> 00:24:39,936
I know who it is now.

647
00:24:39,937 --> 00:24:41,229
It's all over.

648
00:24:41,230 --> 00:24:42,313
I think it was Bokgil.

649
00:24:42,314 --> 00:24:43,856
I think Bokgil killed someone

650
00:24:43,857 --> 00:24:46,275
based on a misunderstanding,
and my dad dealt with the body.

651
00:24:46,276 --> 00:24:49,529
I think it's close to something like that.

652
00:24:49,530 --> 00:24:52,198
He said he was taking a walk.

653
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:54,826
He heard the sound of someone dying,

654
00:24:54,827 --> 00:24:56,411
but there's no proof
of what happened after.

655
00:24:56,412 --> 00:24:58,664
<i>Most of all, it's suspicious
that he is an assassin.</i>

656
00:24:59,415 --> 00:25:00,623
It was Musoe.

657
00:25:00,624 --> 00:25:02,542
She swung a blade,

658
00:25:02,543 --> 00:25:05,169
and she felt cheated out of a good life

659
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:06,755
<i>so she had plenty of motive to kill.</i>

660
00:25:08,841 --> 00:25:12,510
He confessed that he swung a sword

661
00:25:12,511 --> 00:25:14,971
and there was blood on that garment.

662
00:25:14,972 --> 00:25:17,140
If it was his own blood,

663
00:25:17,141 --> 00:25:18,891
the garment would be torn or something.

664
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:20,978
There was just a bloodstain
around the stomach area.

665
00:25:23,772 --> 00:25:27,358
VOTING COMPLETE

666
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:30,194
[host] <i>Here are the voting results.</i>

667
00:25:30,195 --> 00:25:32,739
<i>Yun Igyeong and Musoe got one vote each.</i>

668
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:35,241
<i>The Traveler also got one vote.
Bokgil got two votes.</i>

669
00:25:35,242 --> 00:25:36,951
- I got two votes!
- <i>Bokgil got the most votes.</i>

670
00:25:36,952 --> 00:25:38,370
I'm the culprit?

671
00:25:38,787 --> 00:25:40,038
I DON'T BELIEVE IT

672
00:25:40,039 --> 00:25:41,415
How could this be?

673
00:25:41,832 --> 00:25:43,416
[host] <i>Bokgil, please stand up</i>

674
00:25:43,417 --> 00:25:46,211
<i>and read the ending scenario.</i>

675
00:25:47,254 --> 00:25:49,213
I cannot believe I'm the culprit.

676
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:50,507
- Are we wrong?
- Darn.

677
00:25:52,760 --> 00:25:53,926
Where is the keyhole?

678
00:25:53,927 --> 00:25:55,344
A BLEARY-EYED ASSASSIN

679
00:25:55,345 --> 00:25:59,307
[Igyeong] It doesn't seem like he is
capable of killing anyone.

680
00:25:59,308 --> 00:26:00,767
[Bokgil] What is this?

681
00:26:00,768 --> 00:26:02,311
THE SCENARIO VARIES DEPENDING
ON WHICH CHARACTER IS ACCUSED

682
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:07,690
"The case took an odd turn
and everything pointed to one person.

683
00:26:07,691 --> 00:26:09,859
<i>His secret relationship with Yun Suyeon,</i>

684
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:12,570
<i>his mysterious actions
on the night of the murder,</i>

685
00:26:12,571 --> 00:26:15,281
<i>and the fact that he was
an assassin sent by Grand Prince Hwiryeong</i>

686
00:26:15,282 --> 00:26:18,242
made everyone see him

687
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:20,662
as the most dangerous suspect,

688
00:26:21,246 --> 00:26:23,707
even though he was not the culprit."

689
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:25,291
HEAVY SIGH

690
00:26:25,292 --> 00:26:27,086
Why, you all…

691
00:26:27,961 --> 00:26:29,213
It wasn't me!

692
00:26:30,422 --> 00:26:32,048
"The truth never came to light,

693
00:26:32,049 --> 00:26:33,634
and everyone's suspicions

694
00:26:34,218 --> 00:26:36,052
brought a person to ruin.

695
00:26:36,053 --> 00:26:38,763
<i>After he was bound up and taken away,</i>

696
00:26:38,764 --> 00:26:40,598
<i>his fate became unknown.</i>

697
00:26:40,599 --> 00:26:45,061
<i>No one believed that he had
been fully devoted to Lady Yun."</i>

698
00:26:45,062 --> 00:26:46,729
Bokgil's love was sincere.

699
00:26:46,730 --> 00:26:47,856
I'm tearing up.

700
00:26:48,524 --> 00:26:51,944
THEN WHO IS THE REAL CULPRIT?

701
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:53,445
"That night,

702
00:26:54,196 --> 00:26:56,572
the person who had slain
Yun Suyeon's real father

703
00:26:56,573 --> 00:26:57,865
was the Traveler."

704
00:26:57,866 --> 00:26:59,200
Ah…

705
00:26:59,201 --> 00:27:00,868
CHILLS

706
00:27:00,869 --> 00:27:02,370
It was the Traveler.

707
00:27:02,371 --> 00:27:04,747
THE CULPRIT WAS THE TRAVELER

708
00:27:04,748 --> 00:27:06,666
[Bokgil] <i>"The King,
disguised as the Traveler,</i>

709
00:27:06,667 --> 00:27:08,877
<i>was the owner
of the bloody sword and handkerchief.</i>

710
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:12,672
<i>He mistook the victim for an assassin
sent by Grand Prince Hwiryeong</i>

711
00:27:12,673 --> 00:27:16,008
<i>and killed Suyeon's real father.</i>

712
00:27:16,009 --> 00:27:18,761
<i>Because Bokgil was unjustly found guilty,</i>

713
00:27:18,762 --> 00:27:21,139
the King departed from the place of exile

714
00:27:21,140 --> 00:27:24,268
while keeping his identity
a secret until the end."

715
00:27:24,685 --> 00:27:27,478
THE TRAVELER LEFT WITHOUT A CARE

716
00:27:27,479 --> 00:27:29,063
You shouldn't overthink this game.

717
00:27:29,064 --> 00:27:30,356
You need to keep it simple.

718
00:27:30,357 --> 00:27:32,108
I kept telling you.

719
00:27:32,109 --> 00:27:34,527
That bloody garment gave him away.

720
00:27:34,528 --> 00:27:36,071
The King isn't dead.

721
00:27:36,655 --> 00:27:37,948
The King is the killer.

722
00:27:38,532 --> 00:27:40,117
He killed the victim
and the blood splattered.

723
00:27:40,951 --> 00:27:42,326
[chuckling] I was so close.

724
00:27:42,327 --> 00:27:44,161
- [Suyeon] Oh, man.
- I told you so!

725
00:27:44,162 --> 00:27:45,371
I didn't think he was the King.

726
00:27:45,372 --> 00:27:47,373
Why would the King
come all this way in person?

727
00:27:47,374 --> 00:27:49,375
- [Musoe] The evidence was clear.
- [Suyeon] It's ridiculous.

728
00:27:49,376 --> 00:27:50,585
Based on the facts…

729
00:27:50,586 --> 00:27:52,003
- But he had no motive.
- Exactly.

730
00:27:52,004 --> 00:27:53,754
My motive actually

731
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:55,965
wasn't to kill that person.

732
00:27:55,966 --> 00:27:59,635
It's just that my life has been
at threat since I was a child.

733
00:27:59,636 --> 00:28:01,262
So you had no idea who he was--

734
00:28:01,263 --> 00:28:02,972
You killed him by accident.

735
00:28:02,973 --> 00:28:04,056
What the heck?

736
00:28:04,057 --> 00:28:06,767
We really overcomplicated it.

737
00:28:06,768 --> 00:28:09,103
[Igyeong] I think this is a key clue.

738
00:28:09,104 --> 00:28:12,273
"He was always on guard
and awoke at the smallest sound."

739
00:28:12,274 --> 00:28:14,817
We might have suspected him
if we had seen this clue,

740
00:28:14,818 --> 00:28:16,319
but no one picked this card.

741
00:28:16,320 --> 00:28:20,239
Despite his motive,
everything else fit perfectly.

742
00:28:20,240 --> 00:28:21,824
They're a bunch of idiots.

743
00:28:21,825 --> 00:28:23,619
You can't just accuse an innocent person.

